      "locked": false,
      "text": "const config = {\n  iceServers: [\n    { urls: 'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302' },\n    {\n      urls: 'turn:turn.myserver.com:3478',\n      username: 'user',\n      credential: 'pass'\n    }\n  ]\n};",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "const config = {\n  iceServers: [\n    { urls: 'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302' },\n    {\n      urls: 'turn:turn.myserver.com:3478',\n      username: 'user',\n      credential: 'pass'\n    }\n  ]\n};",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "E1Hrs6-xG3UOErqrSHEi8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 744.4494720338727,
      "y": -543.8173633706527,
      "width": 788.0953369140625,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 344655674,
      "version": 132,
      "versionNonce": 1473069350,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1750618246495,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "STUN Server\n- Usually, you don’t need to create your own STUN server.\n- There are plenty of free public STUN servers available (like Google's: stun:stun.l.google.com:19302).\n- STUN is relatively simple: it just replies with your public IP and port.\n- Using public STUN servers is common in many WebRTC apps.\n- TURN servers are more critical because they relay media if direct connection fails.\n- TURN involves relaying potentially heavy media traffic → expensive in bandwidth and CPU.\n- You should run your own TURN server or rent one from a provider to ensure reliability and privacy.\n- Public TURN servers are rare or limited/free trials only.\n- can develop TURN with these libraray like -> https://github.com/coturn/coturn",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "STUN Server\n- Usually, you don’t need to create your own STUN server.\n- There are plenty of free public STUN servers available (like Google's: stun:stun.l.google.com:19302).\n- STUN is relatively simple: it just replies with your public IP and port.\n- Using public STUN servers is common in many WebRTC apps.\n- TURN servers are more critical because they relay media if direct connection fails.\n- TURN involves relaying potentially heavy media traffic → expensive in bandwidth and CPU.\n- You should run your own TURN server or rent one from a provider to ensure reliability and privacy.\n- Public TURN servers are rare or limited/free trials only.\n- can develop TURN with these libraray like -> https://github.com/coturn/coturn",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yrkoXk-YUZ5kC_G9x7MVJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 850.511459877727,
      "y": -281.97663582222543,
      "width": 621.0233764648438,
      "height": 380,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1367899686,
      "version": 921,
      "versionNonce": 137933862,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1750620925025,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Steps:\n- find stun server\n- find turn server url\n- create signalling server - >basically a websocket to exchange ice detail across\nserver\n- other websocket -> for messaging. \n- create ice config.\n- user2 host create room -> roomId \n    - UI code get the access of camera\n    - start consuming video stream\n    - send to server with webrtc\n- user1 join that room, create webrtc connection.\n- user1 and user2 client create RTCPeerConnection connection,\n- client on their side, create offer and add local descrition\n- send it to signally server to send to other, \n- when client2 get it add to remoteserver and it again send to answer\n- client1 get that save in remotedescription and they are now connected\n- now would be connected p2p as shown left side\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Steps:\n- find stun server\n- find turn server url\n- create signalling server - >basically a websocket to exchange ice detail across\nserver\n- other websocket -> for messaging. \n- create ice config.\n- user2 host create room -> roomId \n    - UI code get the access of camera\n    - start consuming video stream\n    - send to server with webrtc\n- user1 join that room, create webrtc connection.\n- user1 and user2 client create RTCPeerConnection connection,\n- client on their side, create offer and add local descrition\n- send it to signally server to send to other, \n- when client2 get it add to remoteserver and it again send to answer\n- client1 get that save in remotedescription and they are now connected\n- now would be connected p2p as shown left side\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Waoa3DdBaUZmxJzdWH6qQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2004.2787160610242,
      "y": -1080.1220323070754,
      "width": 792.7196655273438,
      "height": 1150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1588367225,
      "version": 128,
      "versionNonce": 820750425,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752523483556,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "package main\n\nimport (\n        \"fmt\"\n        \"log\"\n        \"net/http\"\n\n        \"github.com/gorilla/websocket\"\n)\n\nvar upgrader = websocket.Upgrader{\n        CheckOrigin: func(r *http.Request) bool { return true },\n}\n\nvar peers = make(map[*websocket.Conn]bool)\n\nfunc handleWS(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n        conn, err := upgrader.Upgrade(w, r, nil)\n        if err != nil {\n                log.Println(\"Upgrade error:\", err)\n                return\n        }\n        defer conn.Close()\n        peers[conn] = true\n        defer delete(peers, conn)\n\n        for {\n                _, msg, err := conn.ReadMessage()\n                if err != nil {\n                        log.Println(\"Read error:\", err)\n                        break\n                }\n                for peer := range peers {\n                        if peer != conn {\n                                peer.WriteMessage(websocket.TextMessage, msg)\n                        }\n                }\n        }\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n        http.Handle(\"/\", http.FileServer(http.Dir(\"./static\")))\n        http.HandleFunc(\"/ws\", handleWS)\n        fmt.Println(\"Server started on :8080\")\n        log.Fatal(http.ListenAndServe(\":8080\", nil))\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "package main\n\nimport (\n        \"fmt\"\n        \"log\"\n        \"net/http\"\n\n        \"github.com/gorilla/websocket\"\n)\n\nvar upgrader = websocket.Upgrader{\n        CheckOrigin: func(r *http.Request) bool { return true },\n}\n\nvar peers = make(map[*websocket.Conn]bool)\n\nfunc handleWS(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n        conn, err := upgrader.Upgrade(w, r, nil)\n        if err != nil {\n                log.Println(\"Upgrade error:\", err)\n                return\n        }\n        defer conn.Close()\n        peers[conn] = true\n        defer delete(peers, conn)\n\n        for {\n                _, msg, err := conn.ReadMessage()\n                if err != nil {\n                        log.Println(\"Read error:\", err)\n                        break\n                }\n                for peer := range peers {\n                        if peer != conn {\n                                peer.WriteMessage(websocket.TextMessage, msg)\n                        }\n                }\n        }\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n        http.Handle(\"/\", http.FileServer(http.Dir(\"./static\")))\n        http.HandleFunc(\"/ws\", handleWS)\n        fmt.Println(\"Server started on :8080\")\n        log.Fatal(http.ListenAndServe(\":8080\", nil))\n}",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
